  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Take the exact same routine operation, and perform it in two different countries. The price difference is almost unbelievable.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "building",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Same operation,",
            "2 countries."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In a universal system, the patient often pays little or nothing directly. In the US, the same procedure can run tens of thousands.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "thennow",
          "kicker": "Same procedure",
          "thenLabel": "Universal system",
          "thenValue": "~$0",
          "nowLabel": "US system",
          "nowValue": "$10,000s",
          "sub": "identical operation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Universal systems spread the cost across everyone through taxes.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-uhc",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · universal health care"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It's not that the surgery is better. The prices are simply set completely differently.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "building",
          "kicker": "same surgery",
          "line": "Only the price differs",
          "sub": "not the medicine"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "How a health system is funded decides who gets the bill.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-healthsys",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · health system"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And the cheaper systems still manage to cover everyone, with no surprise invoice.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "building",
          "big": "covers all",
          "label": "no surprise bill",
          "props": [
            "check",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Americans, by contrast, can face bills that rival a down payment.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-ushealth",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · US health care"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Lifetime healthcare cost per person can top five hundred thousand dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "building",
          "big": "$500K+",
          "label": "lifetime, per person",
